  "definition": "Deforestation monitoring identifies where forest has been converted to another land use, how much area changed and, where evidence permits, the timing, driver and carbon consequence. Satellite imagery supplies repeated regional coverage, but deforestation is a land-use concept. A canopy disturbance becomes a deforestation claim only when the observing system can distinguish permanent conversion from temporary loss and forest management.",
